Note = {ECPR Workshop on European Parliaments: Rediscovering Reforcusing of
   Reinventing, MANNHEIM, GERMANY, MAR, 1999},
Abstract = {This article sets out the main stages in the development of the
   Portuguese parliament over the past two decades. This development has
   been characterised by the growing rationalisation of the internal
   operation of parliament, notably through at? increased role for
   committees, and the greater importance attached to parliamentary
   scrutiny of the executive. Recently: the Portuguese parliament has taken
   important steps in strengthening its links with society and in
   responding to public concerns. Some of the measures discussed in this
   context have helped to support the legitimation function of parliament;
   bur parliament will need better developed resources if it is to act nit
   effective check on rite government.},
