   Democrats control districting and the number Republicans elected in
   states where Republicans control redistricting determine how electoral
   outcomes change if the federal government requires redistricters to
   create majority-minority districts. In where Republicans control
   redistricting, majority-minority mandates weakly decrease the number of
   Republicans elected. In states where Democrats control redistricting, a
   majority-minority mandate does number of Democrats However, if
