Volume = {23},
Number = {3},
Pages = {115-138},
Month = {JUL},
Abstract = {This article provides an overview of the Nordic labour market policies
   targeted to promote employment and reduce open unemployment since the
   early 1980s. Applying a disentangled approach, the goal is to analyse
   the policies of stimulating employment, the policies of influencing
   labour supply?; and, finally, active and passive labour market policies.
   It is argued that the employment crises of the early 1990s were mainly
   caused by domestic factors and, partly as a way to react to the
   challenge, the Nordic countries learned to use labour force supply as a
   policy instrument to combat unemployment. Additionally, the Nordic
   countries choose different ways to adopt to the imperatives of the
   globalised economy, hence, at the beginning of the new millennium.
   Nordic labour market policies are inflict.},
