Number = {2},
Pages = {35+},
Month = {APR},
Abstract = {The wave of health care reform which has come over the systems of
   Western Europe in recent years is partly prompted by fiscal imperatives.
   But both the intensity and the direction of reform are shaped by other
   factors both by the internal characteristics of health care systems as
   well as by the character of surrounding economic and political systems.
   As a result, reforms usually described in the language of market
   liberalism actually involve a complex mixture of market reforms and
   state intervention.},
